==============================================================================================================================
k_dimensional_btfr_two_coefficient -- a_0 read off the HYDROGEN coefficient of a two-coefficient BTFR
==============================================================================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0.  THE RESTATEMENT TEST, EXECUTED -- and it closes
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  v^4 = G M_b a_0  with  M_b = Upsilon L + 1.33 M_HI  gives  v^4 = G a_0 (Upsilon L + 1.33 M_HI)
  and dividing by G and expanding the bracket:  v^4/G = (a_0 Upsilon) L + (1.33 a_0) M_HI.
  THE DERIVATION CLOSES IN ONE LINE.
  [PASS] K0 the restatement test is EXECUTED: the two-coefficient form and v^4 = G M_b a_0 are the same expression, verified numerically to machine precision over three decades of luminosity and hydrogen mass, not argued   (max relative difference 2.22e-16  =>  is_restatement = TRUE)
  => is_restatement = TRUE.  This is the baryonic Tully-Fisher relation with its bracket expanded.  It is
     reported below as a LADDER RUNG (a different estimator on the same relation), never as a new law.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.  THE SAMPLE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  122 SPARC galaxies with Q <= 2, inclination >= 30 deg, >= 6 points, and a quoted V_flat, L_[3.6] and M_HI
  log10 L_[3.6] spans 7.08 to 11.69; gas fraction (at Upsilon = 0.5) 0.02 to 0.95, median 0.41
  collinearity of the two regressors: r(log L, log M_HI) = 0.852 -- the price the proposal named

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.  THE STRUCTURAL FACTOR C, computed per galaxy from its own curve and the kernel  (item 105b)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  v_flat^4 = G M_b a_0 x C with C = nu(y)^2 y epsilon, where y = g_bar/a_0 at the radius where V_flat is
  measured and epsilon = g_bar r^2/(G M_b) folds in the disc geometry and the mass not yet enclosed.  C -> 1 in
  the exact deep-MOND limit.  Computed here from each galaxy's own outermost measured point; because g_bar
  needs Upsilon and Upsilon is what the fit returns, it is iterated to convergence.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.  THE TWO-COEFFICIENT FIT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ---- footing canonical: a_0 = 9.3600e-11 m/s^2, so the predicted gas coefficient is 1.33 a_0 = 1.2449e-10 ----
